From c5b8c7cebc6ec954ed66c7dfa055fc45171d20ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 18:57:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03690/11362] [outer-loop][prototype] just-explore head-to-head
 shim + 25-game offline table (POSITIVE, adversarially audited)

Built a shim driving just-explore's HeuristicAgent (3rd place, arXiv:2512.24156) on OUR offline arcade
(override take_action -> env.step, map levels_completed->FrameData.score; shim-validity replays lp85 L4,
asserts score->4). Full 25-game table vs Carnot's BARE graph_explore_solve_v2, budget 1000, best-of-3.

RESULT: just-explore reaches strictly deeper on 5 games (median-of-3) / 7 (best) where our bare explorer
doesn't: bp35 (UNSOLVED, median L1 vs 0), ft09/m0r0/r11l (median L1 vs 0), vc33 (median L2 vs 1); tu93/
s5i5 best-only. Adversarial audit: every fairness axis biases AGAINST JE except best-of-3 -- Carnot does
a MEASURED ~4x more env interaction (4.2x lp85 / 4.4x bp35) and still loses; JE runs DEGRADED (~960 graph
re-inits = HUD-hash instability; upstream README: fixing it raises 12->17 levels) so this is a strict
LOWER BOUND. Score mapping sound (can't inflate). VERDICT JE_STRATEGY_VALIDATED_extract. Frame as 'JE
schedule beats our BARE explorer', NOT 'beats the live E3AgentPolicy'. Branch only.
